{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"STATUS: NOT STARTED. Unsigned; file impact declared so the plan review can run whenever it is picked up.\n\nThis is NOT an e369 child and does NOT gate that epic — it is a follow-up from cc77\n(`discovered_from`). Recorded so nobody reparents it by analogy with 751e/2b16/88d9, which the\noperator DID rule into e369; those three are DC write-path defects, this is a latent robustness gap.\n\nTHE GAP: cc77 annotated the core reconciler's transport params with the `TicketTransport` port. Four\ncall sites reach for OPT-IN capability members and were resolved with `cast(...)` —\n`dispatch_one.py:465` and `:667` (`add_comment`), `dispatch_one.py:752` (`set_relationship`), and\n`dispatch_apply_phases.py:165` (`add_comment`). A `cast` is a STATIC assertion with no runtime effect,\nand none of those sites checks the capability first — unlike `fetcher.py:553` and `:590`, which gate\nthe same class of optional capability on `hasattr`. So the reconciler is inconsistent with itself.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS MORE NOW THAN BEFORE DC EXISTED: the whole point of the capability protocols is that a\nSECOND backend may legitimately not implement them. The \"only one transport, and it has everything\"\nassumption that made this safe is exactly what Data Center removes. And the failure would be SILENT —\nan `AttributeError` at those sites lands inside a broad `except Exception` on the dispatch path, so the\nmutation is simply never applied and the pass reports success. That is the same shape as d067.\n\nSafe today only because the differ that fills the mutation is capability-gated upstream — a real\ninvariant that NOTHING LOCAL ASSERTS."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785725174050537001,"uuid":"d9f80f45-14ca-46a6-90f7-5c36cab9d7d6"}